# password: the syntax, a wrong old password (a 40-pulse wait), a new one too short, then a change with quotes, which
# keeps case and spaces (one_argument would lower them). The player file is saved with the new hash, and the new
# password logs Knocker back in.
@connect knock
Knocker
psswrd
@return
password
password psswrd
password wrong newpass
@pulse 40
password psswrd abcd
password "psswrd" 'New Pass'
@file ../player/Knocker
quit
@connect again
Knocker
psswrd
@connect third
Knocker
New Pass
@return
score
